---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Interests · Shunkai Xu" page="interests">
<style is:inline slot="head">
.econ{padding-block:var(--s6)}
.econ .cols{align-items:end}
.econ h2{grid-column:1/8;font-size:clamp(29px,3.2vw,47px)}
.econ p{grid-column:8/13;color:var(--ink-2)}
.chart{margin-top:var(--s5);display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(12,minmax(0,1fr));column-gap:24px;align-items:start}
.chart svg{grid-column:1/9;width:100%;height:auto;display:block;touch-action:none;user-select:none;-webkit-user-select:none}
.chart dl{grid-column:9/13;display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:10px 18px;border-top:1px solid var(--ink);padding-top:var(--s4)}
.chart dt{color:var(--muted)}
.chart dd{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;text-align:right}
.chart .grab{cursor:ns-resize}
.chart svg{color:var(--ink)}
.chart .ax{stroke:var(--ink);stroke-width:1}
.chart .grid{stroke:rgba(31,79,216,.12);stroke-width:1}
.chart text{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;fill:var(--muted)}
@media (max-width:860px){.econ h2,.econ p,.chart svg,.chart dl{grid-column:1/-1}.econ p{margin-top:var(--s3)}.chart dl{margin-top:var(--s4)}}
</style>

<main id="main" class="wrap page">
  <div class="head">
    <span class="fig mono">Sheet 5 / Interests</span>
    <h1>Interests</h1>
    <p>What I follow when I'm not practising or coding. Most of it comes back to systems: cars, teams and markets.</p>
  </div>
  <ul class="spec">
    <li><span class="n">01</span><span class="t">Computational economics</span><span class="d">What I want to study. Markets as systems you can model, simulate and test. Try the chart below.</span><span class="m">Next step</span></li>
    <li><span class="n">02</span><span class="t">Formula 1</span><span class="d">Engineering at the limit, decided by strategy. Shanghai's circuit is my home race.</span><span class="m">Follow</span></li>
    <li><span class="n">03</span><span class="t">Football</span><span class="d">Ninety minutes of tactics, with no pause button.</span><span class="m">Follow</span></li>
    <li><span class="n">04</span><span class="t">Algorithms</span><span class="d">Small rules that produce surprising order.</span><span class="m"><a href="/projects">Projects</a></span></li>
  </ul>

  <div class="rule" data-chord="4"><span class="tick">§ 6</span></div>

  <section class="econ">
    <div class="cols"><h2>Find the price</h2><p>Drag either line up or down. The market settles where supply meets demand, and the shaded areas show who gains: buyers in blue, sellers in orange.</p></div>
    <div class="chart">
      <svg id="sd" viewBox="0 0 640 400" aria-label="A supply and demand chart. Drag the lines to move them."></svg>
      <dl>
        <dt class="mono">Price</dt><dd class="mono" id="pp">0</dd>
        <dt class="mono">Quantity</dt><dd class="mono" id="qq">0</dd>
        <dt class="mono">Buyer surplus</dt><dd class="mono" id="cs">0</dd>
        <dt class="mono">Seller surplus</dt><dd class="mono" id="ps">0</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<script>
import '../scripts/site.js';
import '../scripts/interests.js';
</script>
</Layout>
